# Krandal Splenderbelt — cleric

**Identity:** Scott's half-orc, half-human cleric. **Spoilers:** Delvers S1E01. **Evidence:** ASR-provisional; working spelling **Krandal Splenderbelt** comes from matching archived sheet-title evidence, not listened dialogue. ASR aliases include `Crandall`, `Splendorbelt`, `Splunderbelt` and `splender belt`.

## Overview

Krandal is a tall, imposing but even-tempered newcomer to the [Delvers guild](../places/delvers-guild.md). Scott describes him as determined to finish work he has promised, even when others have not been fully candid with him. He prefers **Splenderbelt** or **Sir Splenderbelt**; his first name is for close friends. His devotion to the god rendered `Palor/Paylor` is represented by a large necklace normally tucked beneath his clothes. The deity's spelling remains open.

His serious approach coexists with a fondness for potatoes, difficulty remembering names and an aversion to ceilings that becomes acute after Riley's warning. By the end of his first job he has survived repeated blood-draining attacks, helped seal the farm fissure, received forty gold and accepted a room at the guild. The overnight rest has not been played through.

## Development and relationships

- **~00:03:46–00:09:08:** waits punctually outside with descriptions of his assigned companions, [Koh](koh-spiros.md) and [Evelyn](evelyn-grinkeeper.md).
- **~00:24–00:28:** rejects Snake Island's unpaid proposition and accepts the 120-gold cave posting. Receives badge **404**.
- **~00:54–00:58:** hears the ceiling warning separately from the others, then takes over carrying concrete and water. He shares the warning only around **02:01**.
- **~01:11–01:37:** falls to one HP, receives Evelyn's five-point Lay on Hands, heals her with Cure Wounds and later heals himself to his ten-HP maximum. Kyle corrects the healing modifier during play.
- **~01:32–01:59:** casts Shield of Faith on Evelyn, survives engulfment and kills the darkmantle with Sacred Flame after leaving its darkness. A proposed illumination use of the cantrip is abandoned.
- **~02:13–02:28:** holds Koh's rope and gives Guidance; applies concrete and its sack to the plug, keeping the water container. Agrees Koh should keep the [drift globe](../items/drift-globe.md), accepts his reward and guild accommodation.

## Faith, fallibility and mutual care

Rested and now able to channel divinity, Krandal is drawn toward the higher-paying moon-cultist contract but respects the guild's rule that a job must be undertaken when taken. At Kord's crypt he combines a cleric's pastoral concern with cautious tactics, recognizing the Shadow's vulnerability to sacred radiance. His stubborn confidence has practical limits: the powder revealed an invisible enemy, yet Koh's mistaken attack knocks him down and Evelyn must revive him. He later returns the favor when a Shadow incapacitates her. Though he is quick to forget spell names and companions' names, he repeatedly chooses healing over convenience. He brings both guild-issued and earned supplies into careful use, pours the second cleansing vial, and uses Guidance to help a severely weakened Koh finish the last challenge. A kettlebell blow nearly fells Krandal again, but his half-orc endurance keeps him conscious. [^crypt]

[^crypt]: [S1E02 dossier](../../episodes/S1E02.md), ~00:07–00:12, 00:45–00:52, 01:28–01:54, 02:01–02:04, 02:17–02:20, 02:40–02:42. Source wording and rule adjudications remain ASR-provisional.

## Evidence and open questions

The spell discussions record this table's adjudication; they do not establish a general rules reference. Do not infer remaining slots or full-rest recovery from the incomplete overnight scene. Holy-symbol language does not make any Wastes relic part of this campaign.

